# Line-ending policy for EmberbirdOS.
#
# Several files here are DIGEST INPUTS, not merely readable text: the M2 X1 lock
# and its coverage report are compared byte-for-byte by tools/manifest/verify-lock.py,
# and image/manifest/upstream/SHA256SUMS.txt records sha256 digests taken over the
# captured manifest files exactly as they were fetched. Under the default Windows
# setting (core.autocrlf=true) git stores CRLF content as LF in the blob, so a Linux
# checkout would materialise different bytes than the ones the digests describe - the
# provenance check would then fail on CI for a reason that has nothing to do with
# provenance. These paths therefore opt out of EOL conversion and are stored verbatim.

image/manifest/upstream/** -text
image/manifest/arcadia-x86.pinned.xml -text
image/manifest/lock-coverage.json -text
image/manifest/.lock-checkpoint.json -text

# Captured command transcripts / byte-level evidence: preserve exactly as observed.
docs/evidence/** -text
